  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failing - 500 on `POST /upload`:\n\n* App container `incidentlab-app-1` is `running` `Up 5 seconds` (E1), with `/health` `200 {\"status\":\"ok\"}` (E2). Basic health is OK.\n* App logs show `POST /upload 200 OK` then `POST /upload 500 Internal Server Error` with:\n  `File \"/app/main.py\", line 55, in upload` / `with open(tmp_path, \"wb\") as out:` / `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/data/tmp/14d1b374cfd9d2b6f8feb3dcafaffa28.part'` (E5).\n  This is the failure - symptom is HTTP 500, root cause is write permission to tmp path.\n\nRuled out other causes:\n\n* Dependency: `incidentlab-db-1` is `running` `healthy` (E1)(E9), logs `database system is ready to accept connections` with no error (E10). Not a DB outage.\n* Mount read-only: app runs as `1000:1000` with bind `source /srv/lab-data -> destination /data rw:true` (E4). Mount is writable.\n* Uploads dir itself: `/srv/lab-data/uploads` `owner 1000:1000 mode 0755` `app_user_can_write:true` (E7). Writable.\n* Parent dir: `/srv/lab-data` `owner 1000:1000 mode 0755` `app_user_can_write:true` (E8). Writable.\n* Disk/full: `/srv/lab-data` `use_percent 9.0` `available 410.6 MB` `inode_use 0.2%` (E6). Not full.\n* Restarts seen in `recent_events` (E3) - app and db recreated at `23:53:58` and `23:54:35` - are symptom/recovery attempt, not fix.\n\nConclusion: root cause is permission denied writing temp upload file under `/data/tmp`, i.e. host path `/srv/lab-data/tmp`. Parent `/srv/lab-data` (E8) and `uploads` (E7) are writable and disk has space (E6), DB is healthy (E9)(E10), isolating the problem to the `tmp` subdirectory permissions/ownership for UID `1000` (E4).\n",
